{
  "tema": 5068,
  "slug": "imperfecto-subjuntivo-conjugacion",
  "titulo": "Conjugating the imperfect subjunctive",
  "subtitulo": "Hablara, comiera, viviera; fuera, tuviera, dijera.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "Take the ellos form of the preterite, drop -ron, add -ra, -ras, -ra, -ramos, -ran (or -se, -ses, -se, -semos, -sen). Nosotros gets an accent: habláramos. Any verb irregular in the preterite keeps that irregularity: tuvieron → tuviera.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Every verb, regular or not, follows the same recipe:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "ellos preterite − ron",
            "+",
            "-ra / -ras / -ra / -ramos / -ran"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**hablaron → habla- → hablara**; **tuvieron → tuvie- → tuviera**; **fueron → fue- → fuera**; **dijeron → dije- → dijera**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Nosotros** takes a written accent on the syllable before the ending: **habláramos, comiéramos, fuéramos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "There's a second set of endings, **-se, -ses, -se, -semos, -sen** (**hablase**). They mean the same; in Mexico **-ra** is much more common, and **-se** sounds formal or bookish."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: learn the ellos preterite well and you get this tense for free."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tabla",
      "titulo": "Regular verbs (-ra)",
      "bloques": [
        {
